-- title:
--   Mutual Independence From Independence Of Strict Predecessors
-- statement:
--   Let $\iota$ be a linearly ordered type and let $m_i$ be sigma-algebras on a probability space $(\Omega,P)$. If, for every $i\in\iota$, the sigma-algebra generated by all strict predecessors is independent of $m_i$,
--
--   $$\left(\bigvee_{j<i}m_j\right)\perp m_i,$$
--
--   then the family $(m_i)_{i\in\iota}$ is mutually independent:
--
--   $$\operatorname{iIndep}(m_i)_{i\in\iota}\,P.$$
--
--   This is a general chain criterion for mutual independence and is used to organize Brownian increment independence.
--
